-0850-5dcf-98e6-fc20bcccc216" :question/math-academy-id "q-96745" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the domain ${1,2}?$\n\n- $p:{1,2}\\to R$\n- $q:R\\to [1,2)$\n- $r:[1,2)\\to {1,2}$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is ${1,2},$ the set containing the two numbers $1$ and $2$ only.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $[1,2),$ the interval from $1$ to $2$ (including $1$ but not including $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96745/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96745"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104780/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "03267076-3d3b-5fbe-abb4-e49ff47e30ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104780/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2adf4bca-529f-5c5d-a0a8-1f0a2c2620f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104780/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f3ed7ee9-7247-5e2f-9f96-ea40fceed33d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104780/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4d8b4596-b747-5cfe-907a-09e801147241" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104780/selecti