1007-fef5-56e8-a70d-1438580a8df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-96748" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the domain $[2,4]?$\n\n- $p:{2,4}\\to R$\n- $r:[2,4]\\to {2,4}$\n- $q:R\\to [2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is ${2,4},$ the set containing the two numbers $2$ and $4$ only.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $[2,4],$ the interval from $2$ to $4$ (including $2$ and $4$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbac348b-629f-52a1-9bb3-0d3f8483ff44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104778/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a4128809-363c-51c1-8592-9f3936fee831" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104778/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0f4c0902-125d-54ff-84ad-a0c0be98ff01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104778/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a1b2a44f-9cde-5878-9ef7-9bcd35563794" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104778/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "5227df3f-ab60-55c7-8ac0-fe9bd93c6a77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104778/selectio